exports.description:
Lifecycle. `opening` → `open` is the binding's enter animation (`markOpen`);
`closing` starts the moment a close is decided (the result settles then);
`closed` is the terminal state after `settle` removed the entry.

What happens when the anchor scrolls out of view (O38):
- `hide`: the popup stays open but invisible until the anchor is back (default);
- `close`: the entry closes (reason `programmatic`: nobody pressed anything);
- `keep`: the popup stays visible, held inside the viewport.

Where focus goes when an anchored popover opens:
- `true`: into the popup (its first tabbable element, else the popup itself);
  the popover's default and the kit's default;
- `false`: focus stays where it is (the caret in an editor, the page at load
  for a popover that opens by itself, a map) — for type-ahead menus, tips
  and popups that must not steal focus or scroll the page;
- a ref: that element.
